From 652a34915762e4edbdba2ee70e18545e749ef132 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Arrendondo <brandon.arrendondo@bissell.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 21:29:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] EHT: Fix OOB read in
 hostapd_parse_link_reconf_req_sta_profile()

hostapd_parse_link_reconf_req_sta_profile() only checks the incoming
Multi-Link Reconfiguration per-STA-profile subelement length against
a minimum of sizeof(struct element) + 2 (the id/datalen header plus
the 2-byte sta_control field), then computes:

    sta_info = per_sta_prof->variable;
    if (*sta_info > end - sta_info) {
            ...
            goto out;
    }

sta_info points right after sta_control, i.e., at buf + 4. With the
subelement length at the checked minimum of 4, end == buf + 4 ==
sta_info, so sta_info == end is a valid boundary reached by the
length check alone -- but `*sta_info` dereferences it before the
`end - sta_info` comparison can reject it, reading one byte past the
end of the subelement buffer.

This is reached while hostapd parses an associated MLD station's
Multi-Link Reconfiguration Request subelements
(ieee802_11_rx_protected_eht_action() -> ... ->
hostapd_parse_link_reconf_req_sta_profile()), with the subelement
length taken directly from wire data the station controls.

Reject the subelement when sta_info has no room left before reading
through it.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Arrendondo <brandon.arrendondo@bissell.com>
(cherry picked from commit 652a34915762e4edbdba2ee70e18545e749ef132)
---
 src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c b/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
index d8d06a714..6dd7e67d3 100644
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
@@ -2272,7 +2272,7 @@ hostapd_parse_link_reconf_req_sta_profile(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
 	sta_info_len += nstr_bitmap_size;
 
 	sta_info = per_sta_prof->variable;
-	if (*sta_info > end - sta_info) {
+	if (sta_info >= end || *sta_info > end - sta_info) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "MLD: Not enough room for STA Info");
 		goto out;
 	}
